{"reference":"2 Chronicles 26","book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":26,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"A Repeated Pattern in Judah’s Kings","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The chapter presents Uzziah’s reign within a recurring pattern: seeking the LORD and receiving prophetic instruction are associated with prosperity, while strength can become the setting for unfaithfulness. Uzziah seeks God during Zechariah’s days (vv. 4–5), but later acts corruptly after his heart is lifted up (vv. 16–21).","verse_refs":["2 Chronicles 26:3-21"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_2_chronicles_026_48c26fd229659251a787070c"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}